label ch30_47:
    [   0] m "Do you ever feel like you waste too much time on the internet?"
    [   1] m "Social media can practically be like a prison."
    [   2] m "It's like whenever you have a few seconds of spare time, you want to check on your favorite websites..."
    [   3] m "And before you know it, hours have gone by, and you've gotten nothing out of it."
    [   4] m "Anyway, it's really easy to blame yourself for being lazy..."
    [   5] m "But it's not really even your fault."
    [   6] m "Addiction isn't usually something you can just make disappear with your own willpower."
    [   7] m "You have to learn techniques to avoid it, and try different things."
    [   8] m "For example, there are apps that let you block websites for intervals of time..."
    [   9] m "Or you can set a timer to have a more concrete reminder of when it's time to work versus play..."
    [  10] m "Or you can separate your work and play environments, which helps your brain get into the right mode."
    [  11] m "Even if you make a new user account on your computer to use for work, that's enough to help."
    [  12] m "Putting any kind of wedge like that between you and your bad habits will help you stay away."
    [  13] m "Just remember not to blame yourself too hard if you're having trouble."
    [  14] m "If it's really impacting your life, then you should take it seriously."
    [  15] m "I just want to see you be the best person you can be."
    [  16] m "Will you do something today to make me proud of you?"
    [  17] m "I'm always rooting for you, [player]."
